{
  "note": "Synthetic server frames for what the recording (S11-live) lacks: batched chat with event ids, colours, headline notices, missing fields, other groups, unknown uris and commands, malformed bodies and frames. Each case is one WebSocket frame: tag 0 the command, tag 1 the payload. Command 7's payload is tag 0 pushType 5, tag 1 uri, tag 2 body, tag 3 protocolType 2; command 22's is tag 0 group, tag 1 the items (tag 0 uri, tag 1 body, tag 2 id, 0 when absent); other commands carry an empty payload. A body is \"chat\" (a MessageNotice: tag 0 sender {0 uid, 1 0, 2 nick, 3 0} when uid or nick is given, tags 1 and 2 the channel tid, tag 3 content when given, tag 6 bullet format {0 color, 1 4, 2 0, 3 1} when color is given), \"count\" (tag 0), \"body\" (raw Base64) or empty. \"cutBody\" and \"cut\" drop that many bytes from the end of the body or the frame; \"base64\" is the raw frame. Names and ids are made up.",
